# Copy to .env and fill in values for live-console Playwright e2e.
# Never commit .env (gitignored). `bun run test-e2e` loads only these keys from
# .env (CONSOLE_URL, KUBEADMIN_USER, KUBEADMIN_PASSWORD, SCREENSHOT_DIR).
# Non-empty process env still wins, so CI can inject secrets without a file;
# empty/whitespace process env does not block .env. Optional `export KEY=value`
# is accepted. Any other key, a duplicate key, or a line that is not KEY=value
# fails the run with the file and line number, so a typo is not silently
# dropped and surfaces later as "CONSOLE_URL must be set".
# Unquoted trailing comments need a space before # (`value # note`); quote
# passwords that contain ` #` or leading/trailing spaces.
# Manual alternative: set -a && . ./.env && set +a && bun run test-e2e
#
# `bun run test-e2e` also needs the Playwright chromium build. Install scripts are
# disabled (empty trustedDependencies), so a clean clone has no browser: run
# `bunx playwright install chromium` once before the first live e2e run.
#
# Required:
# CONSOLE_URL: absolute http(s) URL only (no user:pass@host; use KUBEADMIN_*).
# Blank on purpose: an unedited placeholder would run the suite against a host
# that does not exist. Shape: https://console-openshift-console.apps.<domain>
CONSOLE_URL=
KUBEADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Optional:
# KUBEADMIN_USER=kubeadmin
# SCREENSHOT_DIR=../docs/screenshots
# (blank SCREENSHOT_DIR uses docs/screenshots; do not set empty to mean cwd)
